12
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Doctor Who, also referred to as Doctor Who: The Movie or as Doctor Who: The Television Movie or Dr Who in the US
is a 1996 television film continuing the British science fiction television series Doctor Who.

13
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Developed as a co-production between Universal Studios and BBC Worldwide, it premiered on 12 May 1996 on the Canadian television station CITV in Edmonton,
Alberta, Canada, 15 days before its first showing in the United Kingdom on BBC One and two days before being broadcast in the United States on Fox.

14
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
It was theatrically released in some countries.

15
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
The first attempt to revive Doctor Who following its suspension in 1989, it was
intended as a backdoor pilot for a new American-produced Who TV series.

16
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
It introduced Paul McGann as the Eighth Doctor in his only televised appearance as the character until "The Night
of the Doctor" in 2013 (though McGann has portrayed the Doctor also in various audio productions).

17
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:54,000
It also marks the final appearance of Sylvester McCoy as the Seventh Doctor until his cameo appearance in "The Power of the Doctor" in 2022, the only appearance of Daphne Ashbrook as companion
Grace Holloway, and the only onscreen appearance of Eric Roberts's version of The Master, although he has since reprised the role in audio dramas for Big Finish Productions.

18
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Although a ratings success in the United Kingdom, the film did not fare
well on American television and no series was commissioned.

19
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
The series was later relaunched on the BBC in 2005.

20
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The only Doctor Who episodes between the film and the new series were a 1999 spoof, Doctor
Who and the Curse of Fatal Death, and a 2003 animation, Scream of the Shalka.

21
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Although primarily produced by different entities than the 1963–1989 series and intended for an American audience, the producers
chose not to produce a "re-imagining" or "reboot" of the series but rather a continuation of the original narrative.

22
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
The production was filmed in Vancouver, British Columbia and is the
only episode of Doctor Who to be filmed in Canada.

23
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
The film explores themes of cyborg, time travel,
alien, christmas, christmas special.

24
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
The tone is thought_provoking and mind_bending.
